.TH KAKAO 1 "2026-10-16" "kakao-cli 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kakao \- drive the official KakaoTalk Android app over adb
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kakao
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kakao-cli
controls the official KakaoTalk Android app running in redroid (or Waydroid)
through adb UI automation. It does not reimplement the LOCO protocol or decrypt
the local database; it operates the real app. The app is logged in as a tablet
(sub\-device) so it coexists with the user's phone.
.PP
The control client needs only the
.B adb
binary; it reads the screen with
.I uiautomator dump
and acts by resource\-id/coordinate. Korean/Unicode text is entered through the
ADBKeyBoard IME.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine\-readable JSON output.
.TP
.BI \-\-serial " SERIAL"
adb device serial (default: first device).
.TP
.BI \-\-connect " HOST:PORT"
Run \fBadb connect\fR to this target first (e.g. 10.0.0.30:5555).
.TP
.BI \-\-adb " PATH"
Path to the adb binary (default: adb).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Check adb connectivity, the installed app version and current screen.
.TP
.B rooms
List chat rooms with last message, time, member and unread counts.
.TP
.BI "read " "[room|me]"
Read recent messages from a room (or the currently open room).
.B \-\-limit N
caps the count (default 20).
.TP
.BI "send " "room text " \-\-yes
Send a text message to a room.
.B \-\-yes
is required.
.B \-\-home
backgrounds the app afterwards.
.TP
.BI "memo " text
Send a text message to your own chat (\[uB098]\[u C640]\[u C758] \[u CC44]\[u D305]); safe for testing.
.TP
.BI "send-file " "room|me path " \-\-yes
Send an image, video or document (pdf/zip/doc/...). Images and videos go through
the share recipient picker; documents go through the in\-app File picker.
.TP
.BI "poll " "room|me"
Open ONE room and stream its newly\-arrived messages as NDJSON (recommended
receive). Text and media (\fB[Photo]\fR/\fB[Video]\fR) are emitted.
.B \-\-interval SEC
and
.B \-\-limit N
tune polling.
.TP
.BI "pull-media " "dest"
Pull media blobs (sent/received) to a local directory, typed by magic bytes.
.B \-\-new-only
pulls only blobs not seen before (state in \fIdest\fR/.seen.json).
.TP
.B watch
Stream incoming messages via OS notifications. The app must be backgrounded for
notifications to post.
.TP
.B tui
Interactive terminal UI: browse rooms, read live, and send. Tab toggles focus,
arrows/Enter pick a room, type + Enter sends, q quits.
.TP
.B webui
A device console in the browser (stdlib HTTP, no deps). The web UI has no chat
mode \[em] use
.B tui
and the other commands for chat. The live device screen sits in the center:
click/drag to tap/swipe; clicking it routes the keyboard to the device (Korean
via ADBKeyBoard after composition; Backspace/Enter/arrows etc. as allow\-listed
keycodes; Esc releases). Two file managers on the left \[em] device storage
(default
.IR /sdcard/ )
above, the webui host's disk below \[em] copy files between them
.RI ( "adb pull/push" ;
copy only, never move/delete/overwrite; clashes get a
.B \-N
suffix), upload from the browser (button or drag\-and\-drop; streamed, atomic,
.BI \-\-max-upload " SIZE"
default 2G, free\-space check) and download to it (device files streamed with
.IR "adb exec-out cat" ).
.BI \-\-fs-root " PATH"
(default
.IR ~ )
confines the local pane.
.B \-\-host
(default 127.0.0.1) and
.B \-\-port
(default 8800) bind the server. The console is full\-account remote control, so
on a non\-local
.B \-\-host
it is off unless
.B \-\-allow-screen
is given. Console APIs accept only IP\-literal or localhost Hosts plus
.BI \-\-allow-host " NAME"
(DNS\-rebinding guard); control POSTs need JSON and same\-origin, uploads an
.B X\-Kakao\-Op
header. Prefer an SSH tunnel or a private network.
With scrcpy\-server (third party, Apache\-2.0, pinned v5.0.1, sha256\-verified,
downloaded once into
.I ~/.cache/kakao-cli/
or given offline with
.BI \-\-scrcpy-server " PATH" ;
.B \-\-no-scrcpy
disables it) the console shares the clipboard: a device copy shows a toast with
a copy button (auto\-copy option on https/localhost), and Ctrl/Cmd+V on the
screen pastes text into the focused field on the device or uploads pasted
images/files to
.IR /sdcard/Download .
Clipboard text is kept in memory only. The device jar, adb forward and server
process are removed when the web UI stops (SIGTERM/SIGHUP included).
The screen is H.264 video from scrcpy: by default on a scrcpy
.I virtual display
sized to the browser's screen area (CSS px \[mu] devicePixelRatio, dpi
160\[mu]dpr, or
.BR \-\-vd-dpi " device|N" )
with KakaoTalk started on it, following window resizes (flex); the device's own
.I wm size
and
.I wm density
are never changed. When the last viewer leaves (after 5 s) the virtual display
is destroyed and the app returns to the default display.
.B \-\-video-mode mirror
(or the status\-bar toggle) mirrors the default display instead; a virtual
display that does not come up falls back to mirror. Browsers decode with
WebCodecs on https/localhost, MSE (fragmented MP4 muxed by the server) on plain
http, and fall back to screencap PNG.
.BR \-\-video-max-fps ,
.BR \-\-video-bit-rate ,
.B \-\-video-max-size
tune the stream. While the virtual display is up, a lock file on the device makes
UI commands
.RB ( rooms ", " read ", " send ", " poll ", " tui " ...)"
fail with
.I console_busy
(exit 7), because
.I input
taps would land on the wrong display.
.TP
.B track
Poll the whole chat list and emit each room's newest message when it changes.
.SH RECEIVE MODEL
.B poll
is the recommended receive path: it opens one room and streams new messages with
no notification or background dependency, and catches muted rooms.
.B watch
reads OS notifications instead, which requires the app to be backgrounded and
misses muted or focused rooms.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success. Non\-zero with a structured JSON error on failure: 3
.I adb_unavailable ,
4
.I device_not_found ,
5
.I app_not_installed ,
6
.I send_uncertain
(readback could not confirm a send \[em] never auto\-retried),
7
.I console_busy
(the web console has KakaoTalk on its virtual display).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
kakao doctor --connect 10.0.0.30:5555
kakao rooms --json
kakao send "\[u C5C4]\[u B9C8]" "\[u C9D1]\[u C5D0] \[u AC00]\[u B294] \[u C911]" --yes
kakao send-file me ./report.pdf --yes
kakao poll me --interval 3
kakao pull-media ./inbox --new-only
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <dest>/.seen.json
State for \fBpull-media --new-only\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project docs under \fIdocs/\fR; setup in \fIdocs/setup-waydroid.md\fR.
.SH CAVEATS
UI automation breaks when the app layout changes. Running two control sessions
against one device causes UI contention. Unofficial automation may violate
KakaoTalk's terms and risk account restriction \[em] use your own account,
sparingly, at human\-like speed.
